# Build context exclusions.
#
# `server/.env` holds local developer secrets (a localhost DATABASE_URL and a
# session secret). The Dockerfile copies the whole `server/` folder, so without
# this file those values would be baked into the published image. Runtime
# configuration always comes from the platform's environment variables.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist

# Secrets and local environment
.env
**/.env
*.local

# Logs and editor cruft
*.log
logs
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Docs and CI config are not needed in the image
DEPLOYMENT.md
README.md
.github
